From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Pitoiset <samuel.pitoiset@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:39:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] radv: fix the VMA heap size for the descriptor sets
 allocator

The third argument is a size, not an end address. So the heap was
32 bytes larger than the actual BO. This could explain some random
VM faults.

Fixes: 849d41dbf83 ("radv: implement a new descriptor sets allocator")
Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/work_items/15150
Signed-off-by: Samuel Pitoiset <samuel.pitoiset@gmail.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45169>
(cherry picked from commit 920315cf537f302a8ae5624aafdcd696e6bebfe0)

Io: from Mesa main (Valve picked it for steamos-26.05), not in 26.2.5
yet; the .pick_status.json part left out.
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_pool.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_pool.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_pool.c
index ab8a8fd31f6..dfc515069d0 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_pool.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_descriptor_pool.c
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ radv_create_descriptor_pool(struct radv_device *device, const VkDescriptorPoolCr
       pool->host_memory_end = (uint8_t *)pool + size;
    } else {
       if (bo_size) {
-         util_vma_heap_init(&pool->bo_heap, RADV_POOL_HEAP_OFFSET, bo_size + RADV_POOL_HEAP_OFFSET);
+         util_vma_heap_init(&pool->bo_heap, RADV_POOL_HEAP_OFFSET, bo_size);
          pool->bo_heap.alloc_high = false;
       }
    }
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ radv_ResetDescriptorPool(VkDevice _device, VkDescriptorPool descriptorPool, VkDe
 
    if (!pool->host_memory_base && pool->size) {
       util_vma_heap_finish(&pool->bo_heap);
-      util_vma_heap_init(&pool->bo_heap, RADV_POOL_HEAP_OFFSET, pool->size + RADV_POOL_HEAP_OFFSET);
+      util_vma_heap_init(&pool->bo_heap, RADV_POOL_HEAP_OFFSET, pool->size);
       pool->bo_heap.alloc_high = false;
    }
 
